<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-05-05T21:08:24.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "testlesson-intro-to-css-acf1a12b-6d7e-4c4b-a45a-fe0883095ac1",
        "text": "Have you ever wondered what makes a website look so good? How do they get all those colors, fonts, and layouts?",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/de090e96016b7bd9610860b26b29911e-testlesson-intro-to-css-panel-1-565e4d5e-c441-45f8-93fe-571be6a34bc0.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-intro-to-css-7eaad6a0-4632-41b1-90a1-f971ccee745e",
        "text": "That's where **CSS** comes in! It stands for Cascading Style Sheets.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/43111bd6441f0251c6741e01b1156703-testlesson-intro-to-css-panel-2-cbab8ba2-3f31-42b0-9155-3e99ca886676.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-intro-to-css-0c89fbf0-55c0-4fe8-b371-0fe9c2c5e89a",
        "text": "Think of it this way: if HTML is like the basic structure of a house – the walls, rooms, and roof.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/5374cc0c9b81711bb80f51f105d6d450-testlesson-intro-to-css-panel-3-2da7440f-eaba-4311-8a35-d04183c1581d.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "testlesson-intro-to-css-a955bc8a-c065-4e34-b9ee-4630165ad85e",
        "text": "Then CSS is like painting the walls, choosing furniture, and adding all the decorations. It makes the house beautiful and inviting!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/2ebbf27f02de1805f091fcf25f523939-testlesson-intro-to-css-panel-4-bda5ec43-cdac-4930-9009-8d609c63df6a.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      }
    ],
    "generate_prompt": "Introduce CSS as the language for styling webpages, explaining that it makes the page look good. Continue the house analogy, comparing CSS to painting and decorating."
  },
